<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><rss version="2.0"><channel><title>Cloudflare changelogs | Billing</title><description>Cloudflare changelogs for Billing</description><link>https://developers.cloudflare.com/changelog/</link><item><title>Billing, Workers, Durable Objects - Set spending limits for Workers and Durable Objects</title><link>https://developers.cloudflare.com/changelog/post/2026-11-13-spend-management/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://developers.cloudflare.com/changelog/post/2026-11-13-spend-management/</guid><description>
&lt;p&gt;You can now set spending limits for Workers and Durable Objects to help control unexpected usage costs, or receive email alerts while your applications keep running. Support for more products is coming soon.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Use these controls alongside &lt;a href=&quot;https://developers.cloudflare.com/ai-gateway/features/spend-limits/&quot;&gt;AI Gateway spend limits&lt;/a&gt; to manage compute and AI inference costs across your application. AI Gateway supports per-user and per-model budgets for Workers AI and other AI providers, applied to requests routed through your gateway.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Workers and Durable Objects limits apply across your account for the current subscription billing period. Each product has its own spending controls.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div tabindex=&quot;-1&quot; class=&quot;heading-wrapper level-h4&quot;&gt;&lt;h4 id=&quot;set-your-limits-and-alerts&quot;&gt;Set your limits and alerts&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;anchor-link&quot; href=&quot;#set-your-limits-and-alerts&quot;&gt;&lt;span aria-hidden=&quot;true&quot; class=&quot;anchor-icon&quot;&gt;&lt;svg width=&quot;16&quot; height=&quot;16&quot; viewBox=&quot;0 0 24 24&quot;&gt;&lt;path fill=&quot;currentcolor&quot; d=&quot;m12.11 15.39-3.88 3.88a2.52 2.52 0 0 1-3.5 0 2.47 2.47 0 0 1 0-3.5l3.88-3.88a1 1 0 0 0-1.42-1.42l-3.88 3.89a4.48 4.48 0 0 0 6.33 6.33l3.89-3.88a1 1 0 1 0-1.42-1.42Zm8.58-12.08a4.49 4.49 0 0 0-6.33 0l-3.89 3.88a1 1 0 0 0 1.42 1.42l3.88-3.88a2.52 2.52 0 0 1 3.5 0 2.47 2.47 0 0 1 0 3.5l-3.88 3.88a1 1 0 1 0 1.42 1.42l3.88-3.89a4.49 4.49 0 0 0 0-6.33ZM8.83 15.17a1 1 0 0 0 1.1.22 1 1 0 0 0 .32-.22l4.92-4.92a1 1 0 0 0-1.42-1.42l-4.92 4.92a1 1 0 0 0 0 1.42Z&quot;&gt;&lt;/path&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In the &lt;a href=&quot;https://dash.cloudflare.com/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener&quot;&gt;Cloudflare dashboard&lt;span class=&quot;external-link&quot;&gt; ↗︎&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, select your account and go to &lt;strong&gt;Billing&lt;/strong&gt; &amp;gt; &lt;strong&gt;Spend limits&lt;/strong&gt;. Choose a spending limit, notification email, and alert thresholds for Workers or Durable Objects.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For example, configure a $10 Workers spending limit with email alerts at $5 and $9. To receive alerts while your applications keep running, turn off &lt;strong&gt;Block usage&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;img src=&quot;https://developers.cloudflare.com/cdn-cgi/image/onerror=redirect,width=600,height=653,format=webp/_astro/workers-spending-controls.BHHAwbV8.png&quot; alt=&quot;Workers controls with usage blocking at $10, a notification email, and alert thresholds at $5 and $9.&quot; loading=&quot;lazy&quot; decoding=&quot;async&quot; width=&quot;600&quot; height=&quot;653&quot;&gt;
&lt;div tabindex=&quot;-1&quot; class=&quot;heading-wrapper level-h4&quot;&gt;&lt;h4 id=&quot;see-when-a-limit-takes-effect&quot;&gt;See when a limit takes effect&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;anchor-link&quot; href=&quot;#see-when-a-limit-takes-effect&quot;&gt;&lt;span aria-hidden=&quot;true&quot; class=&quot;anchor-icon&quot;&gt;&lt;svg width=&quot;16&quot; height=&quot;16&quot; viewBox=&quot;0 0 24 24&quot;&gt;&lt;path fill=&quot;currentcolor&quot; d=&quot;m12.11 15.39-3.88 3.88a2.52 2.52 0 0 1-3.5 0 2.47 2.47 0 0 1 0-3.5l3.88-3.88a1 1 0 0 0-1.42-1.42l-3.88 3.89a4.48 4.48 0 0 0 6.33 6.33l3.89-3.88a1 1 0 1 0-1.42-1.42Zm8.58-12.08a4.49 4.49 0 0 0-6.33 0l-3.89 3.88a1 1 0 0 0 1.42 1.42l3.88-3.88a2.52 2.52 0 0 1 3.5 0 2.47 2.47 0 0 1 0 3.5l-3.88 3.88a1 1 0 1 0 1.42 1.42l3.88-3.89a4.49 4.49 0 0 0 0-6.33ZM8.83 15.17a1 1 0 0 0 1.1.22 1 1 0 0 0 .32-.22l4.92-4.92a1 1 0 0 0-1.42-1.42l-4.92 4.92a1 1 0 0 0 0 1.42Z&quot;&gt;&lt;/path&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The overview shows each product&apos;s recorded spend, alert thresholds, and pause status. Email alerts notify you without stopping usage. When a spending limit takes effect, Cloudflare blocks the product&apos;s supported operations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;img src=&quot;https://developers.cloudflare.com/cdn-cgi/image/onerror=redirect,width=2006,height=249,format=webp/_astro/spend-management-overview.qnHUshUO.png&quot; alt=&quot;Spend limits overview with Workers marked Services paused and separate spend and threshold indicators for Durable Objects.&quot; loading=&quot;lazy&quot; decoding=&quot;async&quot; width=&quot;2006&quot; height=&quot;249&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To resume usage, raise the limit above current spend, turn it off, or remove it. Usage also resumes when the next billing period starts.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Usage reporting and blocking take time, so recorded spend can exceed a limit. Read about &lt;a href=&quot;https://developers.cloudflare.com/billing/manage/spend-management/#what-counts-toward-a-limit&quot;&gt;what counts toward a limit&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div tabindex=&quot;-1&quot; class=&quot;heading-wrapper level-h4&quot;&gt;&lt;h4 id=&quot;choose-alerts-limits-or-both&quot;&gt;Choose alerts, limits, or both&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;anchor-link&quot; href=&quot;#choose-alerts-limits-or-both&quot;&gt;&lt;span aria-hidden=&quot;true&quot; class=&quot;anchor-icon&quot;&gt;&lt;svg width=&quot;16&quot; height=&quot;16&quot; viewBox=&quot;0 0 24 24&quot;&gt;&lt;path fill=&quot;currentcolor&quot; d=&quot;m12.11 15.39-3.88 3.88a2.52 2.52 0 0 1-3.5 0 2.47 2.47 0 0 1 0-3.5l3.88-3.88a1 1 0 0 0-1.42-1.42l-3.88 3.89a4.48 4.48 0 0 0 6.33 6.33l3.89-3.88a1 1 0 1 0-1.42-1.42Zm8.58-12.08a4.49 4.49 0 0 0-6.33 0l-3.89 3.88a1 1 0 0 0 1.42 1.42l3.88-3.88a2.52 2.52 0 0 1 3.5 0 2.47 2.47 0 0 1 0 3.5l-3.88 3.88a1 1 0 1 0 1.42 1.42l3.88-3.89a4.49 4.49 0 0 0 0-6.33ZM8.83 15.17a1 1 0 0 0 1.1.22 1 1 0 0 0 .32-.22l4.92-4.92a1 1 0 0 0-1.42-1.42l-4.92 4.92a1 1 0 0 0 0 1.42Z&quot;&gt;&lt;/path&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For example, set a $50 spending limit for Workers and a $20 email alert for Durable Objects:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;mermaid&quot;&gt;flowchart LR
    A[&quot;Durable Objects reaches $20&quot;] --&amp;gt; B[&quot;Email alert sent&quot;]
    B --&amp;gt; C[&quot;Usage continues&quot;]
    D[&quot;Workers reaches $50&quot;] --&amp;gt; E[&quot;Spending limit takes effect&quot;]
    E --&amp;gt; F[&quot;New Worker invocations blocked&quot;]
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;div tabindex=&quot;-1&quot; class=&quot;heading-wrapper level-h4&quot;&gt;&lt;h4 id=&quot;set-a-spending-limit-with-the-cf-cli&quot;&gt;Set a spending limit with the cf CLI&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;anchor-link&quot; href=&quot;#set-a-spending-limit-with-the-cf-cli&quot;&gt;&lt;span aria-hidden=&quot;true&quot; class=&quot;anchor-icon&quot;&gt;&lt;svg width=&quot;16&quot; height=&quot;16&quot; viewBox=&quot;0 0 24 24&quot;&gt;&lt;path fill=&quot;currentcolor&quot; d=&quot;m12.11 15.39-3.88 3.88a2.52 2.52 0 0 1-3.5 0 2.47 2.47 0 0 1 0-3.5l3.88-3.88a1 1 0 0 0-1.42-1.42l-3.88 3.89a4.48 4.48 0 0 0 6.33 6.33l3.89-3.88a1 1 0 1 0-1.42-1.42Zm8.58-12.08a4.49 4.49 0 0 0-6.33 0l-3.89 3.88a1 1 0 0 0 1.42 1.42l3.88-3.88a2.52 2.52 0 0 1 3.5 0 2.47 2.47 0 0 1 0 3.5l-3.88 3.88a1 1 0 1 0 1.42 1.42l3.88-3.89a4.49 4.49 0 0 0 0-6.33ZM8.83 15.17a1 1 0 0 0 1.1.22 1 1 0 0 0 .32-.22l4.92-4.92a1 1 0 0 0-1.42-1.42l-4.92 4.92a1 1 0 0 0 0 1.42Z&quot;&gt;&lt;/path&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://developers.cloudflare.com/cf/get-started/&quot;&gt;Install the cf CLI and select your account&lt;/a&gt;, then run this command to set a $50 spending limit for Workers usage in the current billing period:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;figure class=&quot;nb-code-figure&quot; data-nb-lang=&quot;sh&quot;&gt;&lt;pre class=&quot;astro-code astro-code-themes github-light github-dark nb-shiki-c6xiwz&quot; tabindex=&quot;0&quot; data-language=&quot;sh&quot; data-nb-lang=&quot;sh&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;line&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;nb-shiki-1t8gfj&quot;&gt;cf&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;nb-shiki-mdbnqw&quot;&gt; billing&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;nb-shiki-mdbnqw&quot;&gt; spend-policies&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;nb-shiki-mdbnqw&quot;&gt; create&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;nb-shiki-dzsirb&quot;&gt; \&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class=&quot;line&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;nb-shiki-dzsirb&quot;&gt;  --name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;nb-shiki-mdbnqw&quot;&gt; &apos;Workers $50 spending limit&apos;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;nb-shiki-dzsirb&quot;&gt; \&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class=&quot;line&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;nb-shiki-dzsirb&quot;&gt;  --product-id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;nb-shiki-mdbnqw&quot;&gt; workers&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;nb-shiki-dzsirb&quot;&gt; \&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class=&quot;line&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;nb-shiki-dzsirb&quot;&gt;  --enabled&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;nb-shiki-dzsirb&quot;&gt; true&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;nb-shiki-dzsirb&quot;&gt; \&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class=&quot;line&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;nb-shiki-dzsirb&quot;&gt;  --threshold-cents&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;nb-shiki-dzsirb&quot;&gt; 5000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;nb-shiki-dzsirb&quot;&gt; \&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class=&quot;line&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;nb-shiki-dzsirb&quot;&gt;  --action&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;nb-shiki-mdbnqw&quot;&gt; usage_block&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The amount is in US cents: &lt;code&gt;5000&lt;/code&gt; means $50. To set a spending limit for Durable Objects, use &lt;code&gt;--product-id durable_objects&lt;/code&gt; and update the name. Limits count usage already recorded in the current billing period.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You can also give this prompt to your coding agent. It will ask which product you want to manage and what spending limit to set, then use the CLI to configure it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;button type=&quot;button&quot; data-nb-button class=&quot;group inline-flex w-max shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full font-medium whitespace-nowrap no-underline shadow-xs transition-colors select-none focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-ring focus-visible:outline-offset-2 disabled:cursor-not-allowed disabled:opacity-50 bg-card text-foreground ring ring-border hover:bg-accent hover:ring-border-strong h-10 gap-2 px-4 text-sm copy-prompt-btn group/copy cursor-copy&quot; data-prompt=&quot;Help me set a Cloudflare spending limit using the cf CLI. Read https://developers.cloudflare.com/billing/manage/spend-management/cli/ and https://developers.cloudflare.com/billing/manage/spend-management/ first. Ask me which account and product (Workers or Durable Objects) I want to manage and what spending limit in US dollars I want to set. Wait for my answers; do not choose a limit for me. Use https://developers.cloudflare.com/cf/get-started/ to help me install cf and sign in if needed. Inspect existing policies before creating or updating a limit. Explain what the limit blocks and that it includes spend already recorded this billing period. Convert my chosen dollar amount to cents, apply the limit with cf, and verify the saved settings.&quot; data-tooltip=&quot;Set a spending limit with your agent&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;inline-flex items-center gap-2.5 text-base font-medium&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;relative flex h-5 shrink-0 items-center justify-start gap-[3px]&quot; aria-hidden=&quot;true&quot;&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://developers.cloudflare.com/icons/agents/claude/light.svg&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; class=&quot;block h-5 w-5 dark:hidden&quot; loading=&quot;lazy&quot; decoding=&quot;async&quot;&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://developers.cloudflare.com/icons/agents/claude/dark.svg&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; class=&quot;hidden h-5 w-5 dark:block&quot; loading=&quot;lazy&quot; decoding=&quot;async&quot;&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://developers.cloudflare.com/icons/agents/codex/light.svg&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; class=&quot;block h-5 w-5 dark:hidden&quot; loading=&quot;lazy&quot; decoding=&quot;async&quot;&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://developers.cloudflare.com/icons/agents/codex/dark.svg&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; class=&quot;hidden h-5 w-5 dark:block&quot; loading=&quot;lazy&quot; decoding=&quot;async&quot;&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://developers.cloudflare.com/icons/agents/cursor/light.svg&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; class=&quot;block h-5 w-5 dark:hidden&quot; loading=&quot;lazy&quot; decoding=&quot;async&quot;&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://developers.cloudflare.com/icons/agents/cursor/dark.svg&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; class=&quot;hidden h-5 w-5 dark:block&quot; loading=&quot;lazy&quot; decoding=&quot;async&quot;&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://developers.cloudflare.com/icons/agents/opencode/light.svg&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; class=&quot;block h-5 w-5 dark:hidden&quot; loading=&quot;lazy&quot; decoding=&quot;async&quot;&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://developers.cloudflare.com/icons/agents/opencode/dark.svg&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; class=&quot;hidden h-5 w-5 dark:block&quot; loading=&quot;lazy&quot; decoding=&quot;async&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;group-data-[copied=true]/copy:hidden&quot;&gt;Copy prompt&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;hidden group-data-[copied=true]/copy:inline&quot;&gt;Prompt copied!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/button&gt;&lt;script type=&quot;module&quot; src=&quot;https://developers.cloudflare.com/Users/kbalter/Projects/cloudflare-docs/src/components/CopyPromptButton.astro?astro&amp;type=script&amp;index=0&amp;lang.ts&quot;&gt;&lt;/script&gt;
&lt;div tabindex=&quot;-1&quot; class=&quot;heading-wrapper level-h4&quot;&gt;&lt;h4 id=&quot;use-spending-limits-alongside-budget-alerts&quot;&gt;Use spending limits alongside budget alerts&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;anchor-link&quot; href=&quot;#use-spending-limits-alongside-budget-alerts&quot;&gt;&lt;span aria-hidden=&quot;true&quot; class=&quot;anchor-icon&quot;&gt;&lt;svg width=&quot;16&quot; height=&quot;16&quot; viewBox=&quot;0 0 24 24&quot;&gt;&lt;path fill=&quot;currentcolor&quot; d=&quot;m12.11 15.39-3.88 3.88a2.52 2.52 0 0 1-3.5 0 2.47 2.47 0 0 1 0-3.5l3.88-3.88a1 1 0 0 0-1.42-1.42l-3.88 3.89a4.48 4.48 0 0 0 6.33 6.33l3.89-3.88a1 1 0 1 0-1.42-1.42Zm8.58-12.08a4.49 4.49 0 0 0-6.33 0l-3.89 3.88a1 1 0 0 0 1.42 1.42l3.88-3.88a2.52 2.52 0 0 1 3.5 0 2.47 2.47 0 0 1 0 3.5l-3.88 3.88a1 1 0 1 0 1.42 1.42l3.88-3.89a4.49 4.49 0 0 0 0-6.33ZM8.83 15.17a1 1 0 0 0 1.1.22 1 1 0 0 0 .32-.22l4.92-4.92a1 1 0 0 0-1.42-1.42l-4.92 4.92a1 1 0 0 0 0 1.42Z&quot;&gt;&lt;/path&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The &lt;a href=&quot;https://developers.cloudflare.com/changelog/post/2026-04-13-billable-usage-dashboard-and-budget-alerts/&quot;&gt;budget alerts introduced earlier this year&lt;/a&gt; notify you about account-wide usage costs without stopping usage. You can keep using them alongside the new product-specific spending limits and email alerts for Workers and Durable Objects.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To configure account-wide alerts, go to &lt;strong&gt;Billing&lt;/strong&gt; &amp;gt; &lt;strong&gt;Billable Usage&lt;/strong&gt; or follow the &lt;a href=&quot;https://developers.cloudflare.com/billing/manage/budget-alerts/&quot;&gt;budget alerts guide&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Read the &lt;a href=&quot;https://developers.cloudflare.com/billing/manage/spend-management/&quot;&gt;spending limits and alerts guide&lt;/a&gt; to learn how spending limits work and manage limits and alerts through the dashboard or cf CLI.&lt;/p&gt;</description><pubDate>Fri, 13 Nov 2026 00:00:00 GMT</pubDate><product>Billing</product><category>Billing</category><category>Workers</category><category>Durable Objects</category></item><item><title>Billing, Workers - Budget alerts now on by default for Pay-as-you-go accounts</title><link>https://developers.cloudflare.com/changelog/post/2026-06-15-budget-alerts-default-on/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://developers.cloudflare.com/changelog/post/2026-06-15-budget-alerts-default-on/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;We are turning on budget alerts by default for eligible Pay-as-you-go accounts. If your account does not already have a budget alert, Cloudflare will create one for you with a $10 account-level threshold. Your default alert will enable at the turn of your next billing cycle, so it will not fire based on usage you have already incurred.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are rolling this out in cohorts over the coming weeks, so eligible accounts may see their default alert appear at different times.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The default alert behaves exactly like an alert you would create yourself. When your cumulative usage-based spend this cycle reaches the threshold, you receive an email notification. The alert is informational only. It does not cap your usage or impact your account in any way.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Usage is processed once per day for the prior day&apos;s activity, so budget alerts fire the day after the threshold is reached rather than in real time.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Budget alerts only consider spend on usage-based products. Recurring subscription fees, such as the Workers Paid plan fee or other monthly plan charges, are not included in the threshold calculation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You can change the threshold, add additional alerts, or remove the default alert entirely from &lt;strong&gt;Manage Account&lt;/strong&gt; &amp;gt; &lt;strong&gt;Billing&lt;/strong&gt; &amp;gt; &lt;strong&gt;Billable Usage&lt;/strong&gt;, or from your Notifications settings. If you already configured your own budget alert, nothing changes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Enterprise contract accounts are not in scope.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For more information, refer to the &lt;a href=&quot;https://developers.cloudflare.com/billing/manage/budget-alerts/&quot;&gt;Budget alerts documentation&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description><pubDate>Mon, 20 Jul 2026 00:00:00 GMT</pubDate><product>Billing</product><category>Billing</category><category>Workers</category></item><item><title>Billing - Modernized Billing Profile with new payment options</title><link>https://developers.cloudflare.com/changelog/post/2026-05-21-modernised-billing-profile/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://developers.cloudflare.com/changelog/post/2026-05-21-modernised-billing-profile/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;The &lt;a href=&quot;https://developers.cloudflare.com/billing/get-started/update-billing-info/&quot;&gt;Billing Profile&lt;/a&gt; now has a modern UI and a single space that unifies billing information, payment method management and an enhanced subscriptions view under a single &lt;strong&gt;Subscriptions&lt;/strong&gt; tab.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div tabindex=&quot;-1&quot; class=&quot;heading-wrapper level-h4&quot;&gt;&lt;h4 id=&quot;what-changed&quot;&gt;What changed&lt;/h4&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;anchor-link&quot; href=&quot;#what-changed&quot;&gt;&lt;span aria-hidden=&quot;true&quot; class=&quot;anchor-icon&quot;&gt;&lt;svg width=&quot;16&quot; height=&quot;16&quot; viewBox=&quot;0 0 24 24&quot;&gt;&lt;path fill=&quot;currentcolor&quot; d=&quot;m12.11 15.39-3.88 3.88a2.52 2.52 0 0 1-3.5 0 2.47 2.47 0 0 1 0-3.5l3.88-3.88a1 1 0 0 0-1.42-1.42l-3.88 3.89a4.48 4.48 0 0 0 6.33 6.33l3.89-3.88a1 1 0 1 0-1.42-1.42Zm8.58-12.08a4.49 4.49 0 0 0-6.33 0l-3.89 3.88a1 1 0 0 0 1.42 1.42l3.88-3.88a2.52 2.52 0 0 1 3.5 0 2.47 2.47 0 0 1 0 3.5l-3.88 3.88a1 1 0 1 0 1.42 1.42l3.88-3.89a4.49 4.49 0 0 0 0-6.33ZM8.83 15.17a1 1 0 0 0 1.1.22 1 1 0 0 0 .32-.22l4.92-4.92a1 1 0 0 0-1.42-1.42l-4.92 4.92a1 1 0 0 0 0 1.42Z&quot;&gt;&lt;/path&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The &lt;strong&gt;Subscriptions&lt;/strong&gt; tab brings billing information, payment method management, and your subscriptions together in one place. The payment management and &lt;strong&gt;Pay overdue balances&lt;/strong&gt; flows now use the latest checkout as product purchase flows, so you can pay with Apple Pay, Google Pay, Link, and &lt;a href=&quot;https://developers.cloudflare.com/billing/payment-methods/instant-bank-payments-link/&quot;&gt;Instant Bank Payments via Link&lt;/a&gt; alongside cards and PayPal.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;New cards complete 3D Secure authentication when the issuer requires it — for example, the EU under PSD2 and India under RBI.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;img src=&quot;https://developers.cloudflare.com/cdn-cgi/image/onerror=redirect,width=909,height=676,format=webp/_astro/2026-05-21-modernised-billing-profile.D6PysUnl.png&quot; alt=&quot;Modernized Billing Profile with the Subscriptions tab&quot; loading=&quot;lazy&quot; decoding=&quot;async&quot; width=&quot;909&quot; height=&quot;676&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For details, refer to the &lt;a href=&quot;https://developers.cloudflare.com/billing/&quot;&gt;Billing Home&lt;/a&gt; documentation.&lt;/p&gt;</description><pubDate>Thu, 21 May 2026 00:00:00 GMT</pubDate><product>Billing</product><category>Billing</category></item></channel></rss>